  "id": "COMPOUND:25800 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a relationship between the compound [(1S,3S)-3-hydroxy-4-[(3E,5E,7E,9E,11Z,13E,15E)-18-[(1S,4S,6R)-4-hydroxy-2,2,6-trimethyl-7-oxabicyclo[4.1.0]heptan-1-yl]-3,7,12,16-tetramethyl-17-oxooctadeca-1,3,5,7,9,11,13,15-octaenylidene]-3,5,5-trimethylcyclohexyl] acetate and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This relationship is supported by multiple independent pathways, all of which point to the compound as a target of several drugs. These drugs, including 2,4,6-trihydroxy-3-(3,3-dimethylallyl)acetophenone, (+)-vouacapenic acid, and 4,5-dihydro-2-methyl-3(2H)-furanone, are known to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The consistent involvement of Phosphodiesterase 6C as a target in all three pathways underscores the compound's potential to modulate this complex. The evidence is robust, with a final score of 0.4738, indicating a plausible but not certain mechanistic link. The compound's role in inhibiting the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex is likely mediated through its interaction with Phosphodiesterase 6C, which is a key component of the complex. The integration of multiple pathways and the presence of a well-documented mode of action support the conclusion that the compound may act as a modulator of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex.",
